Use these 10 questions to build a complete company profile.

1. What are the basic details of your company?  
   Include the company name, year founded, industry, business type, location, short introduction, and detailed company description.

2. How would you describe your brand identity?  
   Share your logo file or link, brand title/tagline, preferred colors, and languages. What are your company’s mission, vision, and core values?

3. Who founded and currently leads the company?  
   Provide the names and brief introductions of the founder, co-founders, current CEO, and key team members. How many employees do you have?

4. What products or services do you offer?  
   List your main products or services, categories, descriptions, photos, prices or price ranges, and most popular offerings.

5. How can people contact your company?  
   Provide your business phone number, WhatsApp number, email address, office/showroom address, Google Maps link, and business hours.

6. Where can people find your company online?  
   Share the links to your website, Facebook Page, Facebook Group, LinkedIn, X (Twitter), and Instagram. Include YouTube, TikTok, or other platforms if available.

7. Who are your current customers and target audiences?  
   Describe your existing customers and approximate customer count. Include your target audience’s age range, location, interests, budget, needs, and main problems.

8. Why should customers choose your company?  
   Explain your main strengths, unique benefits, key competitors, and what makes you different. Include verified customer reviews, notable clients, achievements, awards, or certifications where available.

9. How does your purchasing or service process work?  
   Explain how customers order or book, accepted payment methods, service areas, delivery times and charges, return/refund policies, warranties, and customer support options.

10. What are your plans for growing the company?  
    Describe your goals for the next 1–3 years, planned products or services, new markets, marketing channels, estimated growth budget, and main challenges. What support does your company need most right now?

For any information you do not have yet, write “Not available” or “Not decided yet.”